# L §7.6 item 2, §8.3 LOAD-LIMIT, E §3.1 (tally 2.1.6, P30 on T's SR-T2 of #89): a range whose ends are literals is
# seen at load, so 0..1000000 (1 000 001 keys) is refused at load whatever the asks: here only q is asked, and many,
# which steps through it, isn't. 2.1.6's first refcore (522a715) raised it only when many was asked, so q answered 1.
# Twin: L7_6_literal_range_edge_unasked (1..1000000 loads).
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-02
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-01-05

source s "s"

input x: int

ask q: x

ask many: max(k for k in 0..1000000)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  x = 1
=== expect q
refused: LOAD-LIMIT 0 .. 1 000 000 holds more than 1 000 000 keys (m.tally:13)
